/* -------------------------------------------------------------------
 * wrom3 -- SS_1p6V_100C
 * AUTO-GENERATED by scripts/rom_char/gen_rom_lib.py -- DO NOT EDIT
 *
 * The OpenRAM ROM compiler does not write a .lib; this file was built
 * from the LEF pins plus the circuit structure extracted from wrom3.sp.
 *
 * Model: precharged NAND-style (series chain) ROM, NO output latch.
 *   clk0 = 0 -> bitlines precharge (dout0 all ones)
 *   clk0 = 1 -> evaluate; the selected cells discharge the bitline
 *   worst case through ~77 series NMOS (column 10);
 *   dout0 valid 38.696 ns later
 *   dout0 becomes INVALID when clk0 falls. The consumer must either
 *   sample on clk0's falling edge, or drive the macro with an inverted
 *   clock (clk0 = ~clk) and capture on the system clock's rising edge.
 *
 * SOURCE: access/t_pre come from ngspice measurements on real Magic parasitic C + that corner's OWN sky130 models; 134x256 array, worst column 10 (series NMOS 77); front end + periphery power char/periph_{active,idle}_ss.log, bitline char/col10_worst_case_parasitic_ss.log, back end + slew char/backend_ss_*.log, leakage char/col10_leak_ss.log, column energy char/col10_energy_ss.log
 * -- THIS corner (SS_1p6V_100C) was simulated separately with its own
 * sky130 model files (tt/ss/ff); no fixed scaling factor was used.
 * Measurement showed that this matters: the old SS x1.85 assumption was
 * 33% optimistic against the x2.76 that was actually measured.
 * Without --access/--t-pre this script falls back to analytic defaults
 * (based on a wrong NOR model) -- for sign-off ALWAYS call it with
 * measured values, i.e. through regen_rom_libs.sh.
 *
 * ACCESS IS THE SUM OF THREE TERMS (all measured):
 *   clk0 -> precharge/wordline : 1.4668 ns
 *   precharge -> bitline 50%   : 38.6963 ns
 *   bitline -> dout0           : 0.4356 .. 1.1282 ns (vs output load)
 *   TOTAL (worst load)         : 41.2913 ns
 * Earlier versions had only the MIDDLE term; the front end and the
 * back end (bitline inverter + 256:32 column mux + output buffer) were
 * MISSING.
 * Output transition time MEASURED: 1.7587 .. 2.5036 ns
 *
 * POWER MODEL: internal_power on clk0 is ENERGY PER CYCLE (pJ);
 * the power tool applies the frequency (P = E*f*activity).
 *   when "cs0"  = 86.9927 pJ  (read: column array + periphery)
 *   when "!cs0" = 2.8446 pJ  (IDLE: cs0 only gates the
 *     precharge; the clk_int tree, the address buffers, the row
 *     decoder and 134 wordlines switch even when deselected.
 *     Leave this block out and OpenSTA silently scores it 0.)
 * ----------------------------------------------------------------- */
library (wrom3_SS_1p6V_100C) {
    delay_model : "table_lookup";
    time_unit : "1ns";
    voltage_unit : "1V";
    current_unit : "1mA";
